DejaVu Sans Mono (and Liberation Mono as a fallback)
----------------------------------------------------

The three generated font tables

    shared/gfx/gfx_font8x16.c
    shared/gfx/gfx_font16x28.c
    shared/gfx/gfx_font_num24x30.c

contain glyph bitmaps rasterised from DejaVu Sans Mono by tools/gen_font.py.
They are therefore derived from that font's outlines, and its terms travel with
them.

  DejaVu fonts are based on the Bitstream Vera fonts:
    Bitstream Vera Fonts Copyright (c) 2003 by Bitstream, Inc.
    All Rights Reserved.  Bitstream Vera is a trademark of Bitstream, Inc.
  Changes made by the DejaVu project are released into the public domain.
  Additional Arev fonts changes are Copyright (c) 2006 by Tavmjong Bah.

  The full Bitstream Vera Fonts Copyright, which is the licence these bitmaps
  are used under, is distributed with the font itself and is published at
  https://dejavu-fonts.github.io/License.html

If tools/gen_font.py falls back to Liberation Mono, the resulting tables are
derived from that font instead, which is licensed under the SIL Open Font
License 1.1.

**No font file is redistributed by this repository.** The generator reads a
font from the machine it runs on; only the rendered bitmaps are committed.
Anyone redistributing a build that embeds these tables should ship the full
licence text of whichever font produced them alongside it.


Design and protocol references
------------------------------

No third-party source code is vendored in this tree. The following informed the
design and were read as documentation rather than copied:

  ArduPilot IOMCU     the two-processor split and the watchdog ratio
  YGE                 the OpenYGE material the specification here is written
                      from
  BLHeli / BLHeli_S, AM32, ESCape32, VESC, Hitec
                      published protocol descriptions and configurator
                      behaviour

Every protocol implementation here is written from a published specification
rather than from another implementation, because nearly every open
implementation of these protocols is GPL or AGPL against this repository's MIT.
The programming protocol of KST and Chaservo servos has no published
specification: it is written from wire captures (see Trademarks below).

test/host/greatest.h is a 108-line test harness written for this project. It is
not the `greatest` library of the same name.


